PROVIDER API REGISTRATION
=========================
How providers register their APIs on AgentMesh with true wallet ownership.


METHOD 1 — Frontend MetaMask (recommended, true ownership)
-----------------------------------------------------------
The provider signs the transaction with their own wallet.
Their address becomes the on-chain owner and payment receiver.
No backend involvement needed.

Your teammate implements this in the provider portal using Wagmi:

  import { useWriteContract } from "wagmi"
  import APIRegistryABI from "./APIRegistry.json"  // from packages/contracts/out/

  const { writeContract } = useWriteContract()

  // Called when provider submits the registration form
  function registerAPI(name, endpoint, pricePerCall) {
    writeContract({
      address: REGISTRY_ADDRESS,   // from GET /config → contracts.registry
      abi: APIRegistryABI.abi,
      functionName: "registerAPI",
      args: [name, endpoint, BigInt(pricePerCall)],
    })
  }

  // Example: register a weather API at $0.001 per call
  registerAPI(
    "My Weather API",
    "https://myserver.com/weather",
    1000  // 0.001 USDC (6 decimals)
  )

Result:
  - Provider's MetaMask wallet = on-chain owner
  - Payments route to provider's wallet automatically
  - Provider can update price / deactivate from their wallet
  - apiId returned in transaction receipt (APIRegistered event)


METHOD 2 — Backend endpoint with providerAddress (testing / agents)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
Gateway signs the tx but payment routing is specified explicitly.
Use this for testing or when MetaMask is not available.

  POST /registry/register
  Content-Type: application/json

  {
    "name": "My Weather API",
    "endpoint": "https://myserver.com/weather",
    "pricePerCall": 1000,
    "providerAddress": "0xYourWalletAddress"
  }

Note: Gateway is still the on-chain owner (can update/deactivate).
      providerAddress is used for payment routing only.
      For full ownership, use Method 1.


METHOD 3 — cast send (CLI, for testing)
----------------------------------------
  cast send <REGISTRY_ADDRESS> \
    "registerAPI(string,string,uint256)" \
    "My Weather API" \
    "https://myserver.com/weather" \
    1000 \
    --private-key <YOUR_PRIVATE_KEY> \
    --rpc-url https://rpc-hoodi.morphl2.io

Your wallet becomes the on-chain owner. Full ownership.


HOW PAYMENT ROUTING WORKS
--------------------------
When an agent calls a registered API via /api/v1/call/:apiId:

  1. Gateway reads api.provider from APIRegistry on-chain
  2. requirePayment() uses api.provider as the payment recipient
  3. X402Facilitator.settle() transfers USDC to api.provider
  4. Provider receives 99% of the payment directly to their wallet

The payment goes to whoever is stored as provider in the contract.
If registered via MetaMask → provider's wallet receives payment.
If registered via backend → gateway wallet receives payment (unless providerAddress specified).


GET /config RESPONSE
---------------------
The frontend can get all contract addresses from:

  GET /config

  Response includes:
    contracts.registry    — APIRegistry address
    contracts.facilitator — X402Facilitator address
    contracts.usdc        — MockUSDC address
    network.chainId       — 2910 (Morph Hoodi)
    network.rpcUrl        — https://rpc-hoodi.morphl2.io
